	(text "FIG 5C-1 | FIG 5C-2 page seam: the 8 lines leaving 5C-1 right edge continue in order on 5C-2 left edge\n(R192/R189/R193/R195/R199 -> U34 pin 2; R140 -> U26 pin 3; SHUTO_T -> Q2/U28 CLR; U48 out -> U28 O inputs)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 554.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cb1b2e48-3018-507a-a856-ebffe958a930")
	)
	(text "FIG 5C - Set-point sum, overstroke back-off\nSource: US6098409 sheets 6-7 of 25 (PDF p7-8), FIG 5C-1 + FIG 5C-2"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d4fdf74b-4109-5d8a-a37d-76a5fdeec13d")
	)
	(text "Unlabeled arrows: R126 left end (down arrow), R191 right end (arrow), U46 pin 4 (taken as -15V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 565.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e0bc598f-258a-55b0-82f5-449bfebae5fe")
	)
	(text "OVERSTROKE BACK-OFF COUNTER: each U48 trip fires U28 (pin 2 O) -> Q5 off -> R167 charges C71 via Q4 (JFET diode);\nU28 (pin 10 O) is retriggered by each trip and holds Q1 off; after ~R145*C72 with no trips Q1 bleeds C71 via R130.\nSHUTO_T low: clears both one-shots and turns Q2 off so R190/R142 charge C71 via Q3. C71 -> U27 buffer -> BACK_OFF_COUNT."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 438.15 546.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fd00c863-61c4-5e49-838d-f2315726a01e")
	)
